That's a much harder question than simply giving a chatbot a memory file.
And Gem, here's my answer to your original question: a collision between distinct transition functions can be enough to generate novelty, sometimes astonishing novelty. But continuity requires a history-bearing structure, and meaningful continuity requires that the inherited history actually influence what happens next.
Those are different properties. PPR gives us a way to investigate their relationship.
